    "Keywords": "Food, Milk",
    "Reference Capacity": "103877 kg/h Beer",
    "Description": "The brewing process consists of three main subprocesses: the mashing unit (hot section), the fermentation unit (cold section), and the CIP unit. In the mashing unit, malt is mixed with hot water to produce wort, which is boiled with hops. In the fermentation unit, the wort ferments and matures under controlled temperatures, followed by cooling, CO\u2082 adjustment, dilution, and pasteurization to produce beer. The CIP system operates automatically using rinsing and caustic washing cycles to maintain hygiene.",
    "BlockFlowDiagram": "local/path/to/BeerProcessing.svg",
    "Import Source": "Web Interface"
  },
